  "hypothesis": "Dynamically sharing complete candidate rows across at most four workers can reduce trial-division latency without synchronization for each prime. Small batches remain serial to avoid thread startup costs.",
  "notes": "The supplied flags omit -fopenmp, so this scheduling experiment uses GCC weak pthread references instead, without requiring additional linker flags. It runs serially when those symbols are unavailable; thread-creation failure leaves outstanding work to existing workers and the caller. No commands or tests were executed.",
